    "sections": [
      {
        "body": "Does reversal candle quality add to strictly prior larger-chart alignment? The retained historical run compares quality-stack candles and one-bar failed pullbacks across ES 5→6, GC 6→10, NQ 10→20 and secondary GC 10→20.",
        "id": "question",
        "kind": "text",
        "title": "Question and scope"
      },
      {
        "body": "Quality-stack alignment improves next-bar colour persistence more consistently than longer runs. A break of the full prior run largely identifies the one-bar pullback structure rather than an independent candle factor. The saved price means are negative before fees and slippage: larger failures outweigh frequent small colour successes.",
